# Web security

**Also follow** `.cursor/rules/security.mdc` — invoke **`security-reviewer`** for auth-heavy or user-generated HTML surfaces.

## Content Security Policy

Ship a **meaningful CSP in production**. Prefer **`nonce-{per-request}`** for scripts instead of blanket **`'unsafe-inline'`** when the stack supports nonces—tune **`connect-src`**, **`frame-src`**, **`img-src`** to real domains—no cargo-cult copy-paste.

## XSS

- No raw untrusted **`innerHTML` / `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`** without sanitization.
- Prefer text nodes or sanitize with a reviewed lib + strict allowlist.

## Third-party scripts

`async` / `defer`; **SRI** from CDNs where applicable; revisit vendored scripts periodically; prefer self-hosted when supply-chain risk dominates.

## Security headers

HSTS (when HTTPS), **`X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`**, frame control, sane **`Referrer-Policy`**, tight **`Permissions-Policy`** baseline—implement via platform (Next middleware, CDN, reverse proxy).

## Forms

CSRF tokens / double-submit cookie / framework defaults **where cookie sessions mutate state**, server-side validation + rate limiting on submits, light bot friction only when warranted.